[{:db/id "q-168033/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "da49ca74-3f86-5e7d-87c4-98f7ad65c42c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168033/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "de779902-6fb8-5499-a0c0-6f14c56115f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168033/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-168033/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168033/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "47c22e0a-8962-596d-a2ce-b7f449d5278f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168033/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3d38b1-e094-5063-83ff-1c65378f92e2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168033/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-168033/field-2/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168033/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b904102f-71fc-5d95-952c-c483e046285d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168033/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "131412c6-86ee-5b16-bbfb-fff028600141" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168033/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-168033/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168033" :question/id #uuid "1c4c0f9d-dbfc-5a9d-8c30-31acfce1c91d" :question/math-academy-id "q-168033" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "From part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$\n\nAlso, from part 2, we have $x=r-q$\n\nTo compute the difference of two vectors, we just subtract each component individually:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r-q & =⟨0,4,3⟩-⟨0,-3,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0-0,4-(-3),3-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,7,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $x=⟨0,7,1⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-168033/field-1" "q-168033/field-2" "q-168033/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f819127-1ab3-5a85-a381-9e30e32884aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168033"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168035/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "04b6d5b3-6cbc-5dc3-807e-6c9f3f770958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168035/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "783b5cc7-43dc-534a-ba87-dd7790dff1f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168035/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-168035/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168035" :question/id #uuid "7ab7fa16-77ad-56db-aa2a-7cf82adf5fc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-168035" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the *exact values* of the magnitudes of vectors $q,$ $r,$ and $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\,q\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\sqrt{13}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,r\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,x\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5\\sqrt{2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q\\cdot r=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The dot product of two vectors given in component form can be computed by summing up the products of corresponding components of vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & ={q}_{x}\\cdot {r}_{x}+{q}_{y}\\cdot {r}_{y}+{q}_{z}\\cdot {r}_{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$ Therefore, the formula for the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =0\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-12+6 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-168035/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68abb4f0-c532-5cb6-882c-dacfe6a945dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168035"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168037/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "781144ec-f720-50b6-bf9e-db551e79f178" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168037/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8651bd79-4a07-59b8-b3ef-7633c1ad5643" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168037/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-168037/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168037/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "087ec9c5-55c2-521d-9e3e-774f031a7ef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168037/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "911eb0a9-06fa-5f85-907c-af8aea84339d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168037/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-168037/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168037/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "03b29e17-4202-5098-a20f-7dcae12f12f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168037/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9f91f2-a62b-5a86-bd70-7924a1acd69e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168037/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-168037/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168037" :question/id #uuid "95e51b90-72e1-5d73-babc-de4eceaa6320" :question/math-academy-id "q-168037" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the *exact values* of the magnitudes of vectors $q,$ $r,$ and $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\,q\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\sqrt{13}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,r\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,x\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5\\sqrt{2}$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q\\cdot r=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-6$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nFind the angle $\\theta $ between vectors $q$ and $r.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\theta =$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $109$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${}^{∘}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe helicopter's pilot wants to consider the effect of a linear transformation $T$ such that $T(r)=⟨-8,17,3⟩$ and $T(3q+r)=⟨10,17,9⟩.$ Find the image of $q$ under the action of $T.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $T(q)=\\,⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kq+hr)=T(kq)+T(hr)=kT(q)+hT(r)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $q$ and $r.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3q+r) & =3T(q)+T(r) \\\\ ⟨10,17,9⟩ & =3T(q)+⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨10,17,9⟩-⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =⟨6,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-168037/field-1" "q-168037/field-2" "q-168037/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168032/field-1/819461cf090a66a05ac2c1d2a70c85eacc0cae720cb45a2cdcb891ce5bac1d57" :answer/id #uuid "76731614-c56c-5245-b0cc-ee103b4b8646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r-q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168032/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "44739811-9cfd-5dd3-8d4e-9b062347608d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168032/field-1/819461cf090a66a05ac2c1d2a70c85eacc0cae720cb45a2cdcb891ce5bac1d57" :answer-field/choices ["q-168032/field-1/819461cf090a66a05ac2c1d2a70c85eacc0cae720cb45a2cdcb891ce5bac1d57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168032" :question/id #uuid "9248a24e-4292-5cb5-b331-1a414ca368e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-168032" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$