cation a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the *exact values* of the magnitudes of vectors $q,$ $r,$ and $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\,q\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,r\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,x\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The magnitude of a vector $a$ with components $⟨{a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}⟩$  can always be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,q\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+9+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,r\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 3, we also have $x=⟨0,7,1⟩.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,x\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+49+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $|\\,q\\,|=\\sqrt{13}$, $|\\,r\\,|=5$ and $|\\,x\\,|=5\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-168034/field-1" "q-168034/field-2" "q-168034/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168034"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168036/field-1/687ba219d8c9b2fa04add76a6cff5858a48aea851ffa07746ca60b9a04b7f2d1" :answer/id #uuid "cb4a8a57-d53e-516f-a8a4-ef13aa698402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "109" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168036/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0a4cb3-128e-52ff-9a2a-1aae80a37b57" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-168036/field-1/687ba219d8c9b2fa04add76a6cff5858a48aea851ffa07746ca60b9a04b7f2d1" :answer-field/choices ["q-168036/field-1/687ba219d8c9b2fa04add76a6cff5858a48aea851ffa07746ca60b9a04b7f2d1"] :db/ensure [: