                     \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the angle $\\theta $ between the vectors, we can rearrange the dot product formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =|\\,q\\,|\\cdot |\\,r\\,|\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{q\\cdot r}{|\\,q\\,||\\,r\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 4, we have $|\\,q\\,|=\\sqrt{13}$ and $|\\,r\\,|=5.$ Also, from part 5, we have $q\\cdot r=-6.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{q\\cdot r}{|\\,q\\,||\\,r\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{\\sqrt{13}\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{5\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{6}{5\\sqrt{13}})≈{109}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-168036/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168036"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
